    <string name="ui_rules">RULES</string>
    <string name="ui_rules_body">The tram rolls along the city line on its own. You do not drive it — you choose its route.\n\nTap a switch lamp to arm that crossover. When the tram reaches the switch, it slides onto the connected track. Only one switch per post can be armed at a time.\n\nGlowing blue capsules sit on the detour tracks. Each one adds charge to the battery, and the battery drains all the time.\n\nServe every stop on the line before the charge runs out. On later lines the stops are numbered — serve them in order; passing a stop too early does nothing.\n\nSpring switches snap back to straight once the tram has passed, so arm them again for the next lap.\n\nFinish with more charge left to earn more stars.\n\nCITY MAP: two or three trams run on one network at once, all of them on the same shared switches and the same shared battery. They roll at different speeds, so a faster tram will catch a slower one — arm a switch in time and send one onto a free track. Two trams on the same track end the run. Serve every stop on the network to finish the route.\n\nDAILY ROUTE: one route is laid out from today\'s date, offline and the same all day. Clear it to bank stars and keep your daily streak going.\n\nTRAM LIVERIES: stars from the lines, the city map and the daily route all add up, and they unlock tram liveries. The livery you pick is painted on your tram in every mode.</string>
